/*
 * Copyright (c) 2026, LexxPluss Inc.
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
 *
 * The top 4 KiB of DTCM, reserved for records that must outlive a reset.
 *
 * WHY THIS IS A FILE AND NOT A COMMENT. The diagnostic images place their forensics blocks at
 * 0x2001F000 and 0x2001F200 on the strength of an observation -- that the application links nothing
 * into DTCM, so its .dtcm sections are empty in every image built so far. That is true, and it is
 * not a reservation: the first translation unit to ask for DTCM would be placed there by a linker
 * that was never told the space was spoken for, and nothing would fail to build.
 *
 * TWO CHANGES, and both are needed. Shrinking the DTCM node takes the top 4 KiB out of the region
 * the linker allocates from, which is what makes it reserved. Declaring FORENSICS over that same
 * range gives the records something to bound themselves against -- because the alternative, which
 * the first version of this overlay shipped, was for them to keep asserting against the DTCM node
 * they had just been moved out of. Every one of those assertions would have failed, and only in the
 * diagnostic configurations, which is exactly the kind of breakage a product-only build does not
 * find.
 *
 * WHAT LIVES THERE. 0x2001F000 the hang record (0x1f4 bytes) and 0x2001F200 the I2C forensics block
 * (0x634 bytes), both DEV only; 0x2001FF00 the watchdog tombstone, 256 bytes, the only one a
 * released image carries. Each asserts its own bounds against FORENSICS.
 *
 * APPLIED BY lexxpluss_apps/CMakeLists.txt to every image rather than named per target, so that a
 * build carrying a forensics record cannot be configured without the reservation that makes it one.
 *
 * COST. Nothing measurable: DTCM holds no application data, so 124 KiB instead of 128 changes no
 * placement. It is written down so a future change that does want DTCM meets the reservation
 * instead of the records.
 */

/ {
	forensics_dtcm: memory@2001f000 {
		compatible = "zephyr,memory-region";
		reg = <0x2001F000 DT_SIZE_K(4)>;
		zephyr,memory-region = "FORENSICS";
		status = "okay";
	};
};

&dtcm {
	reg = <0x20000000 DT_SIZE_K(124)>;
};
